<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josef Wegner</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Josef Wegner is an American Egyptologist at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> who has directed excavations at South Abydos, notably at the mortuary complex of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senusret-iii">Senusret III</a>. In 2014 his team found there the tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senebkay">Senebkay</a>, a previously unknown king of around 1650 BCE, giving strong support to the idea of a separate Abydos Dynasty during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-intermediate-period">Second Intermediate Period</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josef-wegner.jpg" alt="Josef Wegner" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SnowFire · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Josef_W._Wegner_Penn_Museum_February_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
